<title>USA: NYSE Unavailables -.</title>
<headline>NYSE Unavailables -.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said that Keithley Instruments Inc and Coleman Co Inc were unavailable for after hours trade for news.</p>
<p>The NYSE said that Corimon SACA, A.H. Belo Corp and Providence Journal Co were also unavailable for after hours trade.</p>
<p>After the market closed, A.H. Belo said that it would acquire Providence Journal for $1.5 billion.</p>
<p>Coleman said it expects to reports a &quot;small&quot; loss in the third and fourth quarters. The company also said it is withdrawing from the entry level electric pressure washer business.</p>
<p>Keithley said it will consolidate operations and take a $1.12 per share charge in the fourth quarter.</p>
